{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2021-1322","published":"2021-08-20T11:04:33Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:15:56.747551696Z","upstream":["CVE-2021-3497","CVE-2021-3498"],"summary":"gstreamer1-plugins-good security update","details":"GStreamer is a streaming media framework, based on graphs of filters which operate on media data. Applications using this library can do anything from real-time sound processing to playing videos, and just about anything else media-related.  Its plugin-based architecture means that new data types or processing capabilities can be added simply by installing new plugins.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nGStreamer before 1.18.4 might access already-freed memory in error code paths when demuxing certain malformed Matroska files.(CVE-2021-3497)\r\n\r\nGStreamer before 1.18.4 might cause heap corruption when parsing certain malformed Matroska files.(CVE-2021-3498)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"gstreamer1-plugins-good","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/gstreamer1-plugins-good&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.16.2-2.oe1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["gstreamer1-plugins-good-1.16.2-2.oe1.aarch64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-gtk-1.16.2-2.oe1.aarch64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-debuginfo-1.16.2-2.oe1.aarch64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-debugsource-1.16.2-2.oe1.aarch64.rpm"],"noarch":["gstreamer1-plugins-good-help-1.16.2-2.oe1.noarch.rpm"],"src":["gstreamer1-plugins-good-1.16.2-2.oe1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["gstreamer1-plugins-good-debuginfo-1.16.2-2.oe1.x86_64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-1.16.2-2.oe1.x86_64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-debugsource-1.16.2-2.oe1.x86_64.rpm","gstreamer1-plugins-good-gtk-1.16.2-2.oe1.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2021-1322.json"}},{"package":{"name":"gstreamer1-plugins-good","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP2","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/gstrea